From 290fc81e40eaa26ebca63ac3c8a999217daca90b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:22:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd(macos): VR audio region, playback to a headset and
 its microphone back

krun_snd_set_vr_audio() attaches a shared-memory region (two lock-free
SPSC rings of S16 PCM, layout in steamac host/vrhost/include/vraudio.h)
through which a VR host process plays the guest's audio on a headset and
supplies the headset's microphone.

Routing follows the headset, not the attachment: the VR host publishes
what the connected headset offers and a heartbeat. While it reports a
speaker, the CoreAudio render callback also downmixes what it plays to
stereo and appends it to the play ring (the Mac output device stays the
stream's clock, so hw_ptr, FIFO and latency reporting are unchanged;
KRUN_SND_VR_MUTE_LOCAL silences the Mac meanwhile). While it reports a
microphone, capture reads the mic ring instead of a HAL input unit,
paced by the host clock on the pump thread with a 20 ms jitter buffer
and WiVRn's 80 ms backlog limit; a running capture stream switches when
the headset comes or goes. Without a headset, or with a VR host that
stopped beating for a second, the guest's audio is the Mac's again.

Cost without a region: one atomic load per render callback and one
Option check per pump iteration.

Tests: region layout and validation, ring conversion/wrap/overrun,
heartbeat timeout, microphone pacing/priming/resampling/backlog, the
render callback's copy and mute, playback following the headset, a
capture period recorded from the region without touching CoreAudio.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
